o"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"unknown_aaguid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is nullable, where "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means “use this mode’s default” (deny under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"direct_required","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", allow otherwise). A client that only saw the stored "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" would have to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-derive that rule itself to display what the policy actually does — and a security rule"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implemented twice is a security rule that will eventually disagree with itself. So the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server resolves it once, here, and reports both: the admin’s stored intent and its effect."}]}}}